title The rota becomes a grid, six essays come home, and the register gains a meter
prompt reshape the rota, silo what deserves foundations, add the missing ones, put a meter on the Radiant register, and update the loop
think Judged the rota by measurement rather than taste. Its documents run 4 KB to 164 KB, a fortyfold spread, so a slot scheduled a filename rather than attention. LEXICON is a dictionary you look things up in and TAME_GUIDANCE is a shelf you consult; both left the rota and kept their standing.
think Found three entries duplicated by the seed's own first paragraph. KYRI, RADIANT_STYLE, and TWILIGHT_STYLE load every lap before the card, so a rota slot for them was pure repetition. That is the kind of redundancy Keaton felt and could not name from the list alone.
think Chose the 5x3 grid over the twelve-document Rahu-Ketu pairing, and the reason is that the modality axis already carries the polarity. Cardinal and fixed genuinely pull against each other -- open the new thing, hold the line -- with dual as the mediator, so the grid subsumes the pairing and adds a third angle. A five-lap cycle also returns each document once a working day rather than once a fortnight.
think Let the tree nominate its own graduates rather than picking favourites. Three documents carry the phrase foundations graduation on Keaton's word in their own headers, written 20260703 and still waiting forty-nine days later. Three more were already on the rota FROM active-designing, which is itself the evidence they lived in the wrong room. Today's design-rooms test settled all six.
think Swept every inbound reference before moving anything, as the references-are-promises rule asks. Fifty-six living references and a hundred and thirty-five in testimony; repointed the living by rewriting the room segment while preserving each citer's own relativity, and left testimony to the resolver, which recovers all of it by unique basename.
think Wrote the two missing foundations rather than citing them again. Gall's Law appeared in six documents and was argued in none; Conway's Law had zero mentions anywhere. Conway turned out to describe this repository more exactly than any law it already cites -- one durable human and many amnesiac collaborators, with the tree as the only channel between them, which is precisely why the session log, the witness, the card, the stamp, and the three-field ledger all exist.
think Built the negation meter to count by whole field rather than by substring, so accrete-never-break reads as vocabulary rather than as a negative construction. That choice costs twelve hundredths on the worst file and is the honest reading -- a meter should measure the writer's constructions, not the tree's coined terms.
think Proved the enforce leg on a real rule rather than only on the control. Planted negations in design-rooms, watched it rise 1.87 to 2.72 and red by name, restored it, and confirmed the file came back byte-identical.
think Split the loop in two in the seed, since Keaton asked for it and the day had already demonstrated why. The outer loop fires for hours with a fixed prompt, so a specific door written into it goes stale in one lap and then instructs every lap after. The outer names a method; the card names the door; the inner loop holds the judgement and may book, reschedule, split, and reorder -- with the reason recorded, because a reordering with a reason is planning and a silent one is drift.
obs Keaton's ear was right and the number is sharper than the impression. Today's rules read 1.9 to 2.8 negations per hundred words against 0.40 for follow-our-compass -- five times the register, in the rules that teach the register. The cause is structural: law-shaped prose drifts negative because the easiest form a rule can take is a ban.
obs The two new foundations were written at the register they argue for -- Gall at 0.57 and Conway at 1.02, against an advisory mean of 1.05 -- so the exemplars are exemplary rather than merely instructive.
obs The launch recipe cited the rota's shape in both of its printed forms and would have told every lap to read one of twenty-seven documents. Updated in the same round, which is what docs-implementation-sync asks for.
obs One dead relative link inside a graduate points at a folded counsel file. Left as written: its basename carries a one-clock stamp, so it is testimony, and the resolver recovers it by index. The law is mechanical for a reason.
loom rota_before=27 rota_after=15 dead_entries_before=5 dead_after=0 bench=5 cycle_laps=5
loom graduated=6 living_refs_repointed=92 living_files_touched=32 testimony_left=135
loom negation_enforce_files=37 risen=0 advisory_files=66 advisory_mean=1.05 register=0.40
